# Falcon PMS Dashboard System — Client Guide & Training Narrative

> **Implementation status:** For engineering truth (seven dashboards, real-time, profile wiring, go-live checklist), see **[implementation_status.md](./implementation_status.md)**.  
> User profile in dashboard chrome comes from Accounts **`GET /api/v1/users/me/`**. KPI and team data are live from the KPI and Accounts apps.

---

## Part 1: Dashboard roles & access

Q1: How many different dashboards does Falcon PMS provide?
A: Falcon provides **seven role-based dashboards**, each tailored to what that person needs to see and do:

- **Executive Dashboard** — Organization-wide performance, department heatmaps, trends, and strategic alerts.
- **Client Admin Dashboard** — Tenant administration: compliance, pending approvals, missing data, user activity, and KPI breakdown.
- **Super Admin Dashboard** — Platform-wide tenants, system health, subscriptions, billing overview, and audit visibility.
- **Manager Dashboard** — Team performance, pending approvals, drill-down to direct reports.
- **Staff Dashboard** — Personal KPIs, mission status, submissions, and performance history.
- **Dashboard Champion** — Configure dashboards for others, templates, bulk assignment, and target phasing support.
- **Read-Only Dashboard** — View executive, manager, or staff perspectives without making changes (auditors, board observers).

The system selects the correct experience from the user’s role in Accounts. You do not need separate logins for each dashboard type.

---

Q2: Is dashboard data real-time?
A: Yes. Each dashboard maintains a **live WebSocket channel** (`ws/dashboard/<role>/`) that pushes updates when KPI scores change, approvals are pending, or team membership shifts. The UI shows a **Live / Offline** indicator in the sidebar and header.

You can also manually refresh; cached data uses TTLs tuned per role (executive data may cache longer than staff submission status).

---

Q3: Where does the user’s name and photo on the dashboard come from?
A: From the **Accounts profile** — the same record users maintain under My Profile. The dashboard loads `/users/me/` on entry so name, title, avatar, and tenant context are always current.

---

## Part 2: Executive & leadership views

Q4: What can executives see that managers cannot?
A: Executives see **all departments** in the tenant (subject to RBAC), period comparisons, organization trends, and cross-department issue lists. Managers are limited to **their team subtree** via the hierarchy service.

Executives can drill down from a department to teams and individuals; the system verifies the target user is within allowed scope before showing detail.

---

Q5: How does drill-down work?
A: From a scorecard or team list, you select a person or department. The API calls `HierarchyService` to ensure the viewer may access that node, then returns aggregated KPI data for that scope. Drill-down actions are **audited**.

WebSocket action `drill_down` supports interactive navigation without full page reloads.

---

## Part 3: Manager, staff & champion workflows

Q6: How do managers approve KPI submissions?
A: The Manager Dashboard lists **pending approvals** for direct and indirect reports (configurable). Approve or reject via API (`/dashboard/manager/approve/` and `reject/`). Rejected items return to staff with reason codes; approved items flow into score calculation.

---

Q7: What does staff see on “My Dashboard”?
A: Staff see assigned KPIs, traffic-light status, due submissions, mission completion panels, and history. They submit actuals through `/dashboard/staff/submit/` which ties into KPI validation rules.

---

Q8: Who is a Dashboard Champion?
A: A specialist who **designs dashboard layouts** for executives or departments: widget placement, default filters, templates, and bulk KPI assignment. Champions do not bypass validation or approval rules — they configure how data is presented.

---

## Part 4: Administration & platform views

Q9: What is the Client Admin dashboard used for?
A: Tenant operators monitor **compliance %**, users missing submissions, approval queues, and per-user activity. It complements Accounts user management — focused on **performance operations**, not account passwords.

---

Q10: What does the Super Admin dashboard show?
A: Cross-tenant health: active tenants, subscription alerts, platform metrics, and billing summaries. It integrates with the Tenant and Billing apps for live platform operations (not mock counters).

---

## Part 5: Security & CIA

Q11: How is dashboard access secured?
A: Every API uses `IsAuthenticated` plus **dashboard-specific permission classes** (Executive, Client Admin, etc.). Hierarchy checks enforce manager→report boundaries. Throttles prevent refresh and drill-down abuse.

The app is registered in the **Config App Registry** with CIA metadata (Confidentiality / Integrity / Availability) for backup and DR ordering.

---

Q12: Can read-only users export data?
A: Read-only users may use **scheduled exports** where policy allows (`/dashboard/read-only/export/`). Exports respect the same scope as their view (no hidden admin paths).

